# Build context for the RELAY image (docker build -f relay/Dockerfile . — context is the repo root).
# The web image has its own web/.dockerignore; Docker only reads the one at the context root.
#
# The env exclusions are the load-bearing ones. `relay/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, so anything in
# the working tree lands in the build stage — and while the published image is multi-stage and
# carries only the compiled binary, "the secret is only in a discarded stage" is one careless
# `COPY --from` away from being false, on an image that is world-readable. Excluding them at the
# context boundary means they are never in the build at all, which is the only version of this that
# cannot be undone by a later edit.
.git
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Weight, not secrets — a smaller context is a faster build on a shared runner.
node_modules
web/node_modules
web/.next
dist/
*.log
.partyline/
# The compiled CLI, if someone built it locally before the image build.
/partyline
